if ARCH_LINKEDSEMI || COMPILE_TEST

menu "Linkedsemi SoC drivers"

config MCTP_PCIE_LINKEDSEMI
	tristate "MCTP over PCIe VDM transport for Linkedsemi LS2010"
	depends on PCIE_DW_LINKEDSEMI
	help
	  MCTP transport over PCIe vendor-defined messages for the
	  Linkedsemi LS2010 endpoint controller. It exposes a character
	  device compatible with the Aspeed MCTP interface.

	  This support is also available as a module. The module will be
	  called linkedsemi-pcie-mctp.

config ESPI_VW_LINKEDSEMI
	tristate "Linkedsemi LS2010 eSPI virtual wire driver"
	depends on OF && MAILBOX
	help
	  eSPI virtual wire (VW) channel driver for the Linkedsemi LS2010
	  SoC. It exchanges VW messages with the E906 firmware over a
	  mailbox channel and reads the system-event mirror from the shared
	  SRAM window. It exposes the AST2700 aspeed-espi-vw compatible
	  /dev/linkedsemi-espi-vwN ioctl interface plus a
	  /dev/linkedsemi-espi-pltrstnN PLTRST# monitor.

	  This support is also available as a module. The module will be
	  called linkedsemi-espi-vw.

config PCC_LINKEDSEMI
	tristate "Linkedsemi LS2010 Post Code Capture driver"
	depends on OF && MAILBOX
	help
	  Post Code Capture (PCC) driver for the Linkedsemi LS2010 SoC.
	  Post codes written by the host CPU to the eSPI/LPC I/O ports
	  snooped by the E906 firmware are forwarded over a mailbox channel
	  and exposed through /dev/linkedsemi-pccN with the same
	  read(2)/poll(2) semantics as the Aspeed LPC PCC driver.

	  This support is also available as a module. The module will be
	  called linkedsemi-pcc.

config MMBI_LINKEDSEMI
	tristate "Linkedsemi LS2010 MMBI common driver"
	depends on OF
	help
	  Common BMC-side MMBI (Memory Mapped Bus Interface) driver for
	  the Linkedsemi LS2010 SoC. It initializes the MMBI descriptor,
	  the host_ros / host_rws pointer regions and allocates the
	  B2H/H2B buffer space in the shared region provided by a
	  transport driver (eSPI or PCIe), and exposes each channel as
	  /dev/mmbiN-chM with the same read(2)/write(2)/poll(2) semantics
	  as the Aspeed MMBI driver.

	  This support is also available as a module. The module will be
	  called linkedsemi-mmbi.

config ESPI_MMBI_LINKEDSEMI
	tristate "Linkedsemi LS2010 eSPI MMBI driver"
	depends on OF && MAILBOX
	select MMBI_LINKEDSEMI
	help
	  eSPI transport for the Linkedsemi LS2010 MMBI driver. It
	  exchanges MMBI_INFO / MMBI_HOST_INT / MMBI_HOST_RWS_WR messages
	  with the E906 firmware (espi_lpc_host_mmbi.c) over a mailbox
	  channel. After initialization it announces the MMBI region with
	  MMBI_INFO; BMC-to-host interrupts are reported with
	  MMBI_HOST_INT using the virtual wire index/data configured in
	  the device tree.

	  This support is also available as a module. The module will be
	  called linkedsemi-espi-mmbi.

config PCIE_MMBI_LINKEDSEMI
	tristate "Linkedsemi LS2010 PCIe MMBI endpoint function"
	depends on PCI_ENDPOINT
	select MMBI_LINKEDSEMI
	help
	  PCI endpoint function transport for the Linkedsemi LS2010 MMBI
	  driver, modeled after pci-epf-xhci. It maps the MMBI region as
	  BAR0 (create functions/ls_mmbi in the PCI endpoint configfs).
	  BMC-to-host interrupts are raised with pci_epc_raise_irq();
	  host-to-BMC interrupts arrive as a local doorbell interrupt
	  when the host writes the mmbi-intr-offset BAR offset. The
	  doorbell config register block and the local interrupt are
	  described by the "ls_mmbi" child node of the endpoint
	  controller's device tree node.

	  This support is also available as a module. The module will be
	  called linkedsemi-pcie-mmbi.

endmenu

endif
